---
/**
 * src/pages/index.astro
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Root entry point — redirects all visitors to the English home page.
 *
 * Why a redirect instead of content here?
 *   The site supports two languages (/en/ and /ta/). The root path (/)
 *   has no content of its own — it simply routes to the default locale.
 *   A 301 (permanent) redirect tells search engines and browsers that
 *   /en/ is the canonical home page, which also helps with SEO.
 *
 * Future improvement:
 *   Browser language detection (Accept-Language header) could route
 *   Tamil-speaking users directly to /ta/. This requires server-side
 *   rendering (Astro SSR) which is not enabled on this static site.
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 */
 
// 301 = permanent redirect — cached by browsers and search engines.
// Change to 302 only if the redirect is temporary.
return Astro.redirect('/en/', 301);
---